    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0908" n="1742" xml:id="pg1742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1102</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-03T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 3, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1382. For Chadbourne [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 182. Embassy’s 1519, your No. 142, July 6, 6 p.m. We might be willing to
                    consider Spanish boats on South American route calling at some British port for
                    search and bunkers if you consider it advisable. Would like your
                    recommendations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
